Included studies:
<abstract record_id="SYN001" source_type="synthetic">
This synthetic randomized, placebo-controlled trial enrolled 240 adults aged 40 to 75 years with type 2 diabetes. Participants were randomized to metformin (120 participants) or placebo (120 participants) in addition to usual care. The primary outcome was a composite of cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction and stroke at 18 months. The composite outcome occurred in 12 participants receiving metformin and 20 receiving placebo. No confidence interval or p value is reported in this abstract. Baseline cardiovascular risk and treatment adherence are not described.
</abstract>
<abstract record_id="SYN002" source_type="synthetic">
In this synthetic randomized, placebo-controlled trial, 320 adults with type 2 diabetes were randomized equally to metformin or placebo alongside usual care. The primary outcome was cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction or stroke during 18 months. Events occurred in 24 of 160 participants assigned metformin and 16 of 160 assigned placebo. The abstract provides no confidence interval or p value and does not describe baseline cardiovascular risk. Findings from this abstract alone do not establish the cause of the difference.
</abstract>
<abstract record_id="SYN008" source_type="synthetic">
This synthetic randomized placebo-controlled trial enrolled 160 adults with type 2 diabetes, with 80 randomized to each arm. The primary endpoint was myocardial infarction or stroke at 12 months. Six events occurred with metformin and seven with placebo. No confidence interval or p value is reported.
</abstract>

